            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the product. STA-BIL Storage needs 2 ounces per 5 gallons, Lucas Safeguard about 1 ounce, STA-BIL 360 Marine half an ounce, and the concentrates PRI-G and Star Tron about a third of an ounce. Always follow the label of the bottle you have, because doses differ by as much as six times."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a fuel stabilizer for a generator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If the generator sits for more than a month or two between runs, yes. Gasoline oxidizes and ethanol blends absorb moisture, and the deposits that form clog small carburetor jets. A stabilizer added to fresh fuel, plus a five-minute run to get it into the carburetor, is the cheapest insurance that the generator starts during an outage."
