            "text": "Check your owner's manual first, because some makers recommend running the carburetor dry for long storage and others recommend a full tank of stabilized fuel. For a generator you may need at short notice, a full tank of treated fuel is usually more practical, because it is ready to start. Either way, never leave untreated fuel sitting in the carburetor."
          }
