          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For gasoline stored next to a generator, STA-BIL Storage is the simplest right answer: a storage formula with a stated life of up to 24 months and a dose you can pour by eye. PRI-G treats far more fuel per bottle for anyone who keeps a large reserve, and Sea Foam is the one can that also cleans a sluggish small engine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you buy, the habits matter more than the brand. Treat fuel the day you buy it, run the engine for five minutes so the carburetor gets treated fuel, keep cans full and cool, and rotate stored gas about every six months.
          </p>
